hnical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le12ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Purpose Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to talk about the purpose of something, you can use the phrases<span class=\"italic\"> in order/so as to</span> + infinitive or<span class=\"italic\"> for."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">He took the job<span class=\"strong\"> in order to</span> gain more experience.<br> He took the job <span class=\"strong\">so as to</span> gain more experience."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To make a negative statement, you put <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">not</span></span> before the <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">to</span></span> -infinitive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">He took the job in order<span class=\"strong\"> not </span>to miss the opportunity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When using <span class=\"strong\">for</span>, there are some rules to consider:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. to talk about the purpose of an action <br> (for + noun + to-infinitive)<br><span class=\"italic\"> I'<span class=\"strong\">m saving for</span> a new house."}, {"type": "text", "content": "2.  to talk 